{#
  Renders a track's "Practice set" section from content/{track}/_practice-set.json — a flat,
  numbered list of free-response problems (course_schema.json #/definitions/practiceSet), distinct
  from bank-data/*.json's MCQ pools and from chapter blocks[] content. Matches the site's real
  markup exactly, including the existing toggleSol(this) onclick — that JS already lives in
  engine.js and is unchanged; this partial doesn't reimplement the show/hide behavior.

  The intro <p> is real per-track copy (practiceSet.introText) — a WP12 audit found this partial
  had been hardcoding qudrat's own wording (mentioning "quantitative comparisons", a qudrat-only
  question type) for every track, live and wrong on the already-shipped tahsili page.

  Expects: sectionId (the section's real id, e.g. 'qud-practice' — NOT derived from trackId; must
  match the rail's data-target and any existing URL-hash deep links exactly, see rail.njk),
  practiceSet (the parsed _practice-set.json object, i.e. { introText, items: [...] })
#}
{% set LVL_CLASS = {"Basic": "b", "Intermediate": "i", "Advanced": "a"} %}
<section class="chapter" id="{{ sectionId }}">
  <div class="chead"><span class="cn">§</span><h2>Practice set</h2></div>
  <p>{{ practiceSet.introText }}</p>

  {% for item in practiceSet.items %}
  <div class="problem">
    <div class="ph">
      <span class="pn">{{ item.number }}</span>
      <p class="pq">{{ item.question.en | safe }}</p>
      <span class="lvl {{ LVL_CLASS[item.difficulty] }}">{{ item.difficulty }}</span>
    </div>
    <button class="sol-toggle" onclick="toggleSol(this)"><span class="tw">▸</span> Show solution</button>
    <div class="solution">{{ item.solution.en | safe }}</div>
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
</section>
